course: dictionary
lesson: 12374
title: Cruelly: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Cruelly» is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. Cruel means causing pain or suffering on purpose, or not caring about it. Add -ly and you get the way it is done: «The wicked queen cruelly mocked the poor servant.» She did it in a cruel way.
explain: «Cruelly» can also mean in a way that seems very unfair or unlucky. «The striker was cruelly injured just before the final.» Nobody hurt him on purpose. It was just very bad luck, so cruelly describes how unfair it felt.
explain: To check the meaning, swap in «in a cruel way» or «very unfairly». If the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning. Then ask yourself: was someone trying to hurt, or was it just bad luck?
fact: «Cruelly» is an adverb, so it tells how an action is done.
fact: «Cruel» is the adjective: a cruel person, a cruel joke.
fact: «Cruelly» means in a cruel way, causing pain or suffering on purpose or without caring.
fact: «Cruelly» can also mean in a very unfair or unlucky way.
fact: Treating people or animals cruelly is wrong and may be against the law.
exercise: «The bully cruelly mocked the new girl in front of everyone.» How did the bully treat the new girl? | Politely, with a smile | Quietly, in a whisper | Kindly and gently | *In a cruel way, to hurt her feelings
exercise: «The footballer was cruelly injured just before the final.» What does cruelly suggest here? | *It was very unfair, bad luck | The final was cancelled because of rain | He won the final easily | He was hurt on purpose by a rival
exercise: «The wicked king cruelly ordered the gates to be shut.» Find the word that is the adverb. | king | *cruelly | shut | gates
test: «The cat was cruelly left out in the rain.» What is the best meaning of cruelly here? | *In a cruel way, without caring | Happily, with a song | Slowly and gently | By accident, as a joke
test: «The old tree was cruelly struck by lightning on its 300th birthday.» What does cruelly mean here? | On purpose, to hurt the tree | Happily, with a cheer | Slowly, one branch at a time | *In a very unfair, unlucky way
exam: Which sentence uses cruelly to mean unfair or unlucky? | *«The team was cruelly beaten by one goal in the last minute.» | «The farmer cruelly beat his dog.» | «The girl cruelly hid the ball from her friends.» | «The baby cruelly laughed at the clown.»
